# The starter declares its toolchain as RANGES and ships no lockfile, on purpose - it is a
# shape to copy, not a pinned tree (v1.33.0). But `npm install` in starter/ leaves one behind,
# and until now nothing stopped `git add -A` from committing it: every app scaffolded from that
# checkout would then be born pinned to one machine's resolution on one afternoon. The intent
# lived only in a comment inside a CI file, which is a rule nothing executes. This is the rule.
# An APP does commit its own lockfile - that is the app's fact, made on the app's schedule.
/starter/package-lock.json

# TypeScript's incremental build cache, left behind by any typecheck run in starter/. Exactly
# the same class of accident as the lockfile above: regenerated on every compile, meaningful to
# no reader, and one `git add -A` away from being copied into every scaffolded app as though it
# were source. Ignored for the same reason and by the same rule.
/starter/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# NOT ignored, on purpose - these are the framework working:
# .baselines/       ratchet baselines are COMMITTED. That is what makes them ratchets.
# TEST_SUMMARY.md   the append-only gate log the commit guard greps.
# docs/registers/RUN_LOG.md   the append-only run log. Only .run-log.json (the marker for a
#                   run currently OPEN) is transient - the rows themselves are the record.
